# Getting started

MarkUP is Markdown with directives: named components with a label, attributes and a body.

## Text

Paragraphs are separated by blank lines. Use **bold**, *italic*, `code`,
~~strikethrough~~ and [links](https://example.com). Footnotes work too.[^1]

## Components

Components are written with colons. A block component has an opening fence with a
name and a closing fence:

:::note
This is a note. The body is regular MarkUP.
:::

A label in brackets gives it a title, and attributes go in braces:

:::card[Deploy]{#deploy}
Push to `main` and the site rebuilds.
:::

Nest components by using more colons on the outside:

::::tabs
:::tab[npm]
`npm run build`
:::
:::tab[CLI]
`markup build docs --out site`
:::
::::

Inline components sit inside text: press :kbd[Ctrl+S] to save, :badge[new]{variant=success}.

## Data

Some components take data instead of text:

:::chart{type=pie title="Sample data"}
data:
  Reading: 45
  Writing: 35
  Reviewing: 20
:::

[^1]: Like this one.
